      "value": "@{5c021357a58d0a7e70c3e515|full_name}: Just because \n(and I'm gonna make a presumtion or two here)\nYou and/or your friends don't have issues with your avatars doesn't mean that the avatars don't have problems. \nYou can still have an avatar look absolutley fantastic and not cut someones FPS in half which again I get might not happen for you or your friends but that's not the point, not everyone has an RTX 2080 etc and they shouldn't have to!\nIt's not that hard to optimize you probably already spent a good amount of time on it, what's the harm in a minimum of idk 5 minutes more? and no I'm not saying that 5 minutes is all it takes but for a first step that can sometimes have massive improvements,\n5 minutes (sometimes less) is an easy time investment no?\nFor example for this roughly 5 minutes of time (depending on how well/quickly you can navigate Unity and Blender of course)\nYou could toss your model into Blender then seperate by material and start by decimating the hair, which depending on the style and how \"high quality\" it is you can possibly cut it's poly count in half\n(Like the Asher models hair is originally around 50k alone I think I got it down to 23k without it looking worse or noticebly different)\nThen you can move on to decimating whatever else is on your model this isn't a tutorial/guide\nAnd magic you've gotten rid of theoretical thousands of polys now you merge things back together and throw it back to Unity,\nYour model looks practically the same and isn't as demanding\n5 minutes",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
