      "value": "@{5a95256f54d514123c1f089d|full_name}: \"However it's not exactly easy\" while I completely agree,\nnot only are there things that could totally become automated and theoretically at least if some of \"AI\"/Machine learning things I've seen floating about are any indictation maybe some of them will be soon \n(if someone bothers to make some stuff for VRChat/social vr game asset optimization)\nanyhow if VRChat devs put some time into it not only do I think some auto optimization could look maybe not good but fine/decent\nBut it IMO wouldn't even have to look good it'd just have to give a better idea of the avatar than the default row of fallback avis or the picture of the avatar on the front of a robot\nWhich they could totally do and if, if they're worried about people not being prepared for a slightly mangled avatar that wasn't designed to be Quest they can just have a warning pop up when the user requests to see the avatar in whatever method they go about implementing this\nHave it say something like \"Hi, User, this avatar was not designed to be viewd on Quest, however we can attempt to make a version for you!\" and it should be fine.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
