      "value": "@{5a78cb159e2ef066b2b1f390|full_name}: while you make some valid points, i should mention:\n1: I dont have a 2080, i have a 5ish years out of date RX580 and I still get acceptable framerate with 10 or more very poor avatars\n2: Auto decimate often looks like shit, manual is too hard. Same with texture atlasing but not to the same extent. \n3: Mesh combining is certainly easy most of the time, but sometimes I get this strange issue where a mesh re scales or moves once combined for some reason.",
      "viewerReactions": null
