      "value": "@{5c021357a58d0a7e70c3e515|full_name}: Mhm\nThanks for replying\n1. Nice. Although Very Poor avatars is quite vague (at least to me) so I don't know if you're getting good frames because while your GPU is 5ish years old you have a good/more modern CPU or because while \"Very Poor\" could mean some 300k poly 50 mat avi it could also just mean a \"normal\" one with a few more hundred/thousand polys of the 70k limit.\nPersonally I think that another idk \"Incredibly Poor\" rank could help discussion of performance so there's more distinction, ya know?\n2. IMO it really depends on the avatar some look fine with the button clicks of CATS decimation whereas others need a bit of manual work.\n(Which for me generally means separating by important shapekeys like the face from the rest of the avi and/or separating by material and decimating everything individually)\nto automatic texture atlasing\nYeah I feel CATS/Material Combiner could use some work \nThe UVs they make have so much wasted space a lot of the time\nI think it could be worth it if someone made a thing for CATS that \"just\" makes editing the UV easier like being able to click and drag/resize chunks or groups of stuff in the UV then set it up to redo the texture/bake for you but who knows if or when that'll happen\n3. I think you can fix that by applying all transforms before merging. although that can cause its own issues sometimes, rarely but it can so you might have to then undo and apply transforms only to the meshes that moved or resized but I don't know as I'm not sure if I've had that issue before so.. good luck\nAnyhow thanks again for replying/reading",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
